once a month social workers from Hong  Kong charity group chicken soup  Foundation paid Michelle Nye a visit at  her home  Michelle is a single mother struggling  to get by on a meager income in one of  the world's most expensive cities she  can barely afford the basics for her and  her autistic daughter  the tables and chairs in her home were  donated by the charity  to other people they may be ordinary  things but to me and my daughter it  makes us feel fortunate that somebody  shows us love  chicken soup Foundation mainly supports  single parent families providing  counseling as well as Necessities  including medical supplies  this washing machine was also a recent  donation  since the start of the covid-19 pandemic  many of Hong Kong's poorest are facing  unprecedented hardship  seeing people face such difficulty has  an emotional effect on us too  over the last three years there's been a  big rise in people seeking relief for  charity workers it's been particularly  demanding I see some burnout on staff  there especially during the fifth wave  because at that time we have more than  50 percent of our staff got covered as  well but we still have to serve our  families and that's not the only reason  many Charities are facing Staffing  challenges according to the Hong Kong  social workers General Union as many as  28 of social workers quit their jobs in  the last year many of them left the city  all together because of strict pandemic  curves and political uncertainty forming  a Crackdown on the pro-democracy  movement  Hong Kong's struggling economy as a  result of the pandemic has made  fundraising more difficult also one  survey conducted by a local agency found  a fifth of the organizations that  interviewed had shuttered or suspended  operations  is a platform for the people to help the  society to do good you know for the  community so without this platform I  think there will be a full opportunity  for the people in Hong Kong to to have a  channel to to you know to do good for  this society and the loss of such  organizations means many who have been  struggling here and rely on their help  will find it difficult to get the  support they need Patrick fock Al  Jazeera Hong Kong
 

